[
  {
    "pkheadingid": 821,
    "bookid": 64,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Definition",
    "headingPosition": 1,
    "headingid": 764,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 128226,
        "bookId": 64,
        "chapterId": 355,
        "headingId": 764,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>EBV-associated smooth muscle tumour (EBV-SMT) is an EBV-driven benign smooth muscle neoplasm occurring in the clinical setting of immunosuppression.</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2025-04-25T14:39:12"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 822,
    "bookid": 64,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "ICD-O coding",
    "headingPosition": 2,
    "headingid": 765,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 128227,
        "bookId": 64,
        "chapterId": 355,
        "headingId": 765,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>8897/1 EBV-associated smooth muscle tumour</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2025-04-25T14:39:12"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 823,
    "bookid": 64,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "ICD-11 coding",
    "headingPosition": 3,
    "headingid": 766,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 128228,
        "bookId": 64,
        "chapterId": 355,
        "headingId": 766,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>2F9C &amp; XH00B4 Neoplasms of unknown behaviour of connective or other soft tissue &amp; Smooth muscle tumour, NOS</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2025-04-25T14:39:12"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 824,
    "bookid": 64,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Related terminology",
    "headingPosition": 4,
    "headingid": 767,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 128229,
        "bookId": 64,
        "chapterId": 355,
        "headingId": 767,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p><em>Not recommended:</em> EBV-associated angioleiomyoma; EBV-associated myopericytoma; EBV-associated leiomyosarcoma.</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2025-04-25T14:39:12"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 825,
    "bookid": 64,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Subtype(s)",
    "headingPosition": 5,
    "headingid": 768,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 128230,
        "bookId": 64,
        "chapterId": 355,
        "headingId": 768,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>None</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2025-04-25T14:39:12"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 826,
    "bookid": 64,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Localization",
    "headingPosition": 6,
    "headingid": 769,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 128231,
        "bookId": 64,
        "chapterId": 355,
        "headingId": 769,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>The commonest site of involvement is the CNS, followed by the liver, lung, and subcutaneous tissues of the limbs and trunk {15844077; 16330945; 21437186; 27362573; 31700854; 22175892; 25027306}.</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2025-04-25T14:39:12"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 827,
    "bookid": 64,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Clinical features",
    "headingPosition": 7,
    "headingid": 770,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 128232,
        "bookId": 64,
        "chapterId": 355,
        "headingId": 770,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>When arising in the subcutis, the tumour manifests as a skin-coloured nodule. Occasionally, there may be associated pain {22175892; 12207602; 33245561; 33627249}. Multiple tumours may evolve concurrently or sequentially at different anatomical sites {15844077; 12207602}.</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2025-04-25T14:39:12"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 828,
    "bookid": 64,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Epidemiology",
    "headingPosition": 8,
    "headingid": 771,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 128233,
        "bookId": 64,
        "chapterId": 355,
        "headingId": 771,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>EBV-SMT is a rare neoplasm. It occurs in approximately 1&ndash;5% of patients with immunosuppression {25027306}. The age range varies widely, but most patients are adults. There is a slight female predominance {21437186; 31700854; 2217589; 25318810}.</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2025-04-25T14:39:12"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 829,
    "bookid": 64,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Etiology",
    "headingPosition": 9,
    "headingid": 772,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 128234,
        "bookId": 64,
        "chapterId": 355,
        "headingId": 772,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>Tumorigenesis is driven by EBV2 infection in the setting of immunosuppression related to a congenital immunodeficiency disorder, posttransplant iatrogenic immunosuppression, or HIV infection {25027306; 16330945; 7990861}.</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2025-04-25T14:39:12"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 830,
    "bookid": 64,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Pathogenesis",
    "headingPosition": 10,
    "headingid": 773,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 128235,
        "bookId": 64,
        "chapterId": 355,
        "headingId": 773,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>It is postulated that EBV gains entry into a progenitor smooth muscle cell of vascular origin through CD21 receptor function or interaction with an EBV-infected lymphocyte {16330945; 7990860; 19706821}. There is aberration of the mTOR/AKT pathway {19706821}. Overexpression of <em>MYC</em> has been reported {9890420; 22420456}. Multiple tumours represent separate clonal events {16330945}.</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2025-04-25T14:39:12"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 837,
    "bookid": 64,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Macroscopic appearance",
    "headingPosition": 11,
    "headingid": 780,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 128236,
        "bookId": 64,
        "chapterId": 355,
        "headingId": 780,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>The tumours show circumscription and pink-tan to whitish cut surfaces. They range from 10 to 60&nbsp;mm in size {31700854; 28280632; 20733553; 12207602}.</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2025-04-25T14:39:12"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 831,
    "bookid": 64,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Histopathology",
    "headingPosition": 12,
    "headingid": 774,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 128237,
        "bookId": 64,
        "chapterId": 355,
        "headingId": 774,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>Irrespective of site, the majority of EBV-SMTs show circumscription and interlacing fascicles of spindled myoid cells in a background of collagenous matrix {31700854; 22175892; 33627249; 3324556}. Typically, there is an admixed population of smaller rounded cells and intratumoural lymphocytes. Some tumours show focal myxoid change. Mitotic activity is generally low. However, tumours with leiomyosarcoma-like features showing nuclear atypia and necrosis in addition to high mitotic activity have been described {22175892; 7990860; 25318810}. Some may mimic myopericytoma or angioleiomyoma {25027306; 21437186; 18199115; 22175892}. EBV-SMTs show expression of h-caldesmon, desmin, SMA, and MSA.</p>\r\n<p>Important differential diagnoses include Kaposi sarcoma, leiomyoma, leiomyosarcoma, and a pseudotumour secondary to mycobacterial or fungal infection. None of these entities show nuclear reactivity by in&nbsp;situ hybridization for EBV-encoded small RNA (EBER).</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2025-04-25T14:39:12"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 832,
    "bookid": 64,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Cytology",
    "headingPosition": 13,
    "headingid": 775,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 128238,
        "bookId": 64,
        "chapterId": 355,
        "headingId": 775,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>Not relevant</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2025-04-25T14:39:12"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 833,
    "bookid": 64,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Diagnostic molecular pathology",
    "headingPosition": 14,
    "headingid": 776,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 128239,
        "bookId": 64,
        "chapterId": 355,
        "headingId": 776,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>EBV infection of neoplastic myoid cells is usually demonstrated by in&nbsp;situ hybridization for EBER.</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2025-04-25T14:39:12"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 836,
    "bookid": 64,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Essential and desirable diagnostic criteria",
    "headingPosition": 15,
    "headingid": 779,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 128240,
        "bookId": 64,
        "chapterId": 355,
        "headingId": 779,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p><em>Essential:</em> demonstration of EBV infection in the constituent myoid cells of a smooth muscle tumour arising in an immunosuppressed patient.</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2025-04-25T14:39:12"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 834,
    "bookid": 64,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Staging",
    "headingPosition": 16,
    "headingid": 777,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 128241,
        "bookId": 64,
        "chapterId": 355,
        "headingId": 777,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>Not relevant</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2025-04-25T14:39:12"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 835,
    "bookid": 64,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Prognosis and prediction",
    "headingPosition": 17,
    "headingid": 778,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 128242,
        "bookId": 64,
        "chapterId": 355,
        "headingId": 778,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>Although the prognosis is generally favourable, it is dependent upon immune status, irrespective of tumour morphology {16330945; 25027306; 15844077}.</p>",
        "timestamp": "2025-04-25T14:39:12"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  }
]